ent  and campaigned on social media to save  the statue  buddhist associations as far away as  malaysia  have protested against its demolition  but to no avail  xi'an is an ancient capital of china  tourists from all over the world come to  see its historic sites  including its buddhist heritage but in  recent years  the government has pushed for a revival  of communist ideology  even inside datsun temple a world famous  buddhist heritage site  a sign reminds visitors to uphold  socialist  values  it's not only buddhism but also  christianity  and islam the chinese government is  putting immense pressure on religions  buddhism is treated more leniently  because the government considers it to  be more in line with their norms  but i've witnessed myself the pressure  they're putting on buddhist temples  and that activity is increasing  temples have been forced to cancel  religious events  monasteries have had some of their  buildings demolished  experts estimate that the three-phased  buddha  is just one of up to 800 statues that  have been destroyed in recent years  that story from correspondent matthias  berlinga he joins us from beijing now  for more on this story hamatias  why are we seeing this push now to  destroy these buddhist symbols  we've seen a push for communist ideology  for the ideology of the communist party  in the past few  years we've seen a hardening of the  ideological line within the party  and a great uh push for uh their  ideological  ideology in public discourse so religion  is always  of course something that is in  competition with this ideology that is  atheist and the communist party member  must uh promise to be an atheist cannot  be  member of any religious organization in  theory at least  and uh so what we've seen recently is  that displays of uh spirituality  of religion especially recently like  these 800 buddha statues recently  erected uh the statues uh  uh are being uh torn down are being  demolished uh  to to to to make religion 